// The plugin contract (#564, #660). A plugin is a service on a unix socket
// on each node (#563); carrel-agent calls it and relays operations for the
// control plane. Regenerate internal/pluginpb with internal/pluginpb/gen.sh.
//
// Installed by carrel (#662), a plugin does not open its socket: systemd
// passes the listening socket as fd 3 (LISTEN_FDS=1), and the plugin serves
// this service on it. It runs as a dynamic user and keeps its state in
